Z||000000||batboy||08-15-99||12:33 PM||||The new Pontiac Grand Am now has an optional Ram Air 3.4 V6 (not an overhead cam version) available in their GT model. This engine cranks out 175 hp @ 5,200 rpm and 205 ft-lbs of torque @ 4,000 rpm. I think maybe I'll keep an eye out for a low mileage, wrecked 1999 Grand Am with that engine. Of course you'd have to use the donor ECM, wiring harness, and maybe even keep that nice little 4 speed automatic overdrive tranny. Just think, with a cam change and headers...ahh...
